      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the holes look more like pinpricks than chewed areas, it might suggest sap-sucking pests rather than purely chewing ones, such as thrips or tiny mites. These pests are often most active at night and can leave behind minuscule entry points. Look for fine webbing or sticky residue, which can also be signs of these hidden attackers. Treating with targeted insecticidal soap or neem oil in the early morning or late evening can help manage these nocturnal visitors.",
